From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Howard <lukeh@padl.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] features.h: disable _FORTIFY_SOURCE for Swift Clang importer

When Glibc is configured with _FORTIFY_SOURCE>=1, bits/unistd.h,
bits/string_fortified.h, bits/stdio2.h, bits/socket2.h and friends declare
__fortify_function __attribute_overloadable__ variants of common libc entry
points (read, write, close, memcpy, memmove, memset, strcpy, snprintf, fgets,
open, pread, recv, readlink, ...). Swift's Clang importer surfaces both the
plain declarations and these overloaded variants into the Swift-visible module
and cannot disambiguate bare function references such as

    let (platform_read, platform_write, platform_close) = (read, write, close)

or first-class references like `map(read)` / storing `read` in a variable of
function type, producing "ambiguous use of 'read'" errors. This affects any
Swift-on-Linux package that imports Glibc (or a C-shim module that pulls in
these headers) when Glibc was built with _FORTIFY_SOURCE enabled -- which is
the OpenEmbedded/Yocto default. Swift upstream CI does not exercise this
because the sysroots it uses do not default _FORTIFY_SOURCE.

Gate _FORTIFY_SOURCE off inside features.h when __swift__ is defined. The
__swift__ macro is defined by Swift's Clang importer only (see
swift/lib/ClangImporter/ClangImporter.cpp, which calls
languageVersion.preprocessorDefinition("__swift__", ...)), so this has no
effect on ordinary C/C++/Objective-C compiles of the same headers -- fortify
remains in place at runtime for every non-Swift consumer. Only the Clang
importer pass, which is a pure type-import step and generates no executable
code, sees the plain declarations.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE/Yocto-specific; the proper upstream fix
would be a coordinated change in Swift's Clang importer to handle
__attribute_overloadable__ fortified overloads, or an opt-in glibc feature
macro. This patch is the pragmatic route for building Swift against a
distribution-default fortified Glibc.]

Signed-off-by: Luke Howard <lukeh@padl.com>
---
 include/features.h | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/include/features.h
+++ b/include/features.h
@@ -446,6 +446,13 @@
 # define __USE_GNU	1
 #endif

+/* Swift's Clang importer cannot disambiguate __fortify_function
+   __attribute_overloadable__ declarations from their plain counterparts.
+   Suppress _FORTIFY_SOURCE while the importer is parsing these headers. */
+#if defined __swift__ && defined _FORTIFY_SOURCE
+# undef _FORTIFY_SOURCE
+#endif
+
 #if defined _FORTIFY_SOURCE && _FORTIFY_SOURCE > 0
 # if !defined __OPTIMIZE__ || __OPTIMIZE__ <= 0
 #  warning _FORTIFY_SOURCE requires compiling with optimization (-O)
--
2.43.0
